CORE libcxx
main.cpp
--cpp11 --stdlib libc++
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ cerr good: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ cerr precision: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ cerr unitbuf: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ cerr tied to cout: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ cout precision: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.6\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Fixed: the compiled library defines and constructs the standard stream
objects; provide_standard_stream_objects now defines them, with stream
buffers that discard output and read unknown input, and sets the ties
and unitbuf, before the program's dynamic initialization.
